  "text": "Martian wind and passing dust devils swept its panels clean. Opportunity should have starved within months. Instead, again and again, Martian wind and passing dust devils swept its panels clean. The team called them cleaning events. Each one gave the rover back its power, and it kept driving. 90 days became years. Years became more than 14. Then in 2018, a storm grew until it wrapped the whole planet. The sky over opportunity grew so dark that almost no sunlight reached its panels. On 10 June 2018, Opportunity sent its last signal. Engineers on Earth sent more than a thousand commands over the next eight months, asking it to wake up. It never answered. What finally stopped the most successful rover of its time was not cold or rock. It was",
